messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 171 and 271? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 171 and 271, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then summing the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one below the other for clarity:\n```\n  171\n× 271\n```\nWe'll start by multiplying 171 by 1 (the units digit of 271):\n```\n  171\n×   1\n-----\n  171\n```\nNext, we'll multiply 171 by 70 (the tens digit of 271, which is 7 times 10):\n```\n  171\n×  70\n-----\n 1207\n```\nWe'll write this result below the previous one, aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n  171\n×  70\n-----\n 1207\n```\nFinally, we'll multiply 171 by 200 (the hundreds digit of 271, which is 2 times 100):\n```\n  171\n× 200\n-----\n34200\n```\nWe'll write this result below the previous one, again aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n  171\n× 271\n-----\n34200\n 1207\n 171\n-----\n34200\n 12070\n 1710\n-----\n34200 + 12070 + 1710 = 47980\n```\nAdding these results together, we get:\n```\n  171\n× 271\n-----\n 1207\n 12070\n 1710\n-----\n34200\n 12070\n 1710\n-----\n34200 + 12070 + 1710 = 47980\n```\nTherefore, the product of 171 and 271 is 47980.\n</answer>\n"]
